hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1737","**\nNarrated to us Abu Tahir, narrated to us Abu Bakr, narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi and Ziyad ibn Ayyub, they said: Narrated to us Isma'il, narrated to us Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n*\"Indeed, within the Friday (day) there is an hour in which, if a Muslim stands and prays, asking Allah for good in it, Allah will grant it to him.\"*\n\nThen he (ﷺ) gestured with his hand, saying:\n\n*\"It is a brief and fleeting moment.\"*\n\nBundar said: And he (ﷺ) gestured with his hand, saying: *\"It is a brief and fleeting moment.\"*\n\nWe (the narrators) said: *\"It is a brief and fleeting moment.\"*\n\nIn the narration of Ibn 'Ulayyah, the wording is: *\"Allah will grant it to him.\"*"
